{
  "dom_id": "step-q213250",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A={△,♢,♡}.$\n\n$$\nR={(△,♡),(△,♢),(♢,♡)}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nWe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(△,△){{field-1}}R,\\,(♢,♢){{field-2}}R,\\,(♡,♡){{field-3}}R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n{{field-4}}{{field-5}},\n\nthe relation is\n{{field-6}}.",
  "worked_solution": "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nIn our case, the relation is defined on ${△,♢,♡},$ and we have\n\n$$\n(△,△)\\notin R,\\,(♢,♢)\\notin R,\\,(♡,♡)\\notin R.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(x,x)\\notin R$ $\\text{for all }x\\in A,$ the relation is $\\text{irreflexive}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
